      "knowledge_id": "taac2026-industry-1-queryformer",
      "decision": "used",
      "rationale": "Read exact-version primary arxiv:2609.16548v1 section 4.2 lines 128-192. Unlike the previous declared consideration (latest usage only altered key composition and did not improve the incumbent), this proposal implements a concrete query-refinement intervention. The local motivation is the one-field query restriction and failed attempts to change downstream readout/keys, not an assumption that source pCVR results transfer.",
      "transformed_mechanism": "Reduce pre-retrieval field-query interaction to a single shared zero-start linear residual from the other field, at fixed query norm. Replace it by own-field projection for attribution and compare current-ad versus history-only query sources.",
      "variant_names": [
        "cross_target",
        "self_target",
        "cross_context",
        "self_context"
      ],
      "nearest_work_difference": "Projection-only minimal contrast, not the reported attention-generated bridge, Co-Transformer, sequence re-query, embedding-view scaling or auxiliary delay training. Source advises attention rather than projection alone; this simpler replacement tests whether local cross-field information is useful before adopting that cost. Novelty and source-transfer efficacy remain unverified.",
      "falsifier": "Nonpositive cross_target-minus-self_target, nonpositive factorial specificity, or failure to beat the unrefined incumbent weakens this local adaptation. No result of this small projection test validates or refutes full QueryFormer.",
